From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 6Xkljk8Vj7Tk1k4 <6Xkljk8Vj7Tk1k4@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 10:11:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] gta4xl-common: sepolicy: Camera memory boost, quiet AIDL
 allocator lookup

Opening the camera logs two denials for the camera HAL:

  avc: denied { read write } for comm="binder:768_2" name="mem_boost_mode"
  dev="sysfs" scontext=u:r:hal_camera_default:s0 tcontext=u:object_r:sysfs:s0
  tclass=file permissive=0

  SELinux: avc: denied { find } for pid=768 uid=1047
  name=android.hardware.graphics.allocator.IAllocator/default
  scontext=u:r:hal_camera_default:s0
  tcontext=u:object_r:hal_graphics_allocator_service:s0

/sys/kernel/mm/vmscan/mem_boost_mode is Samsung's kswapd boost: the
camera HAL writes 1 or 2 when it opens a camera so that kswapd reclaims
file pages more eagerly for up to five seconds (the kernel validates
the value and resets it on its own). Samsung's init.exynos9611.rc
already chowns the node to cameraserver for exactly this, but the node
kept the generic sysfs label, so the boost never happened. Label it
sysfs_camera_writable, which only hal_camera_default may write.

The allocator lookup happens on the first buffer allocation in the HAL
process. This device has no AIDL allocator (only gralloc 2.0 HIDL,
which the HAL then uses), so the lookup can only fail; don't audit it,
like the existing default_prop dontaudit in this file.

Verified on the device by compiling the shipped CIL with both rules
added (neverallow checks on) and loading it with load_policy: after
re-instantiating the sysfs inode it carries sysfs_camera_writable,
mem_boost_mode reads 2 right after the camera opens, and neither
denial comes back, also not on the first camera open after restarting
vendor.camera.provider. Both first showed up in a tablet_test.sh run on
the build with patch 0021; the earlier runs, which still had the cass
denial flood, did not log them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sepolicy/vendor/genfs_contexts        | 3 +++
 sepolicy/vendor/hal_camera_default.te | 4 ++++
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sepolicy/vendor/genfs_contexts b/sepolicy/vendor/genfs_contexts
index 4a16964..fd8c4a3 100644
--- a/sepolicy/vendor/genfs_contexts
+++ b/sepolicy/vendor/genfs_contexts
@@ -29,5 +29,8 @@ genfscon sysfs /devices/system/chip-id/revision
 # Firmware
 genfscon sysfs /firmware/devicetree/base/sound/mixer-paths                                                     u:object_r:sysfs_audio:s0
 
+# Kernel
+genfscon sysfs /kernel/mm/vmscan/mem_boost_mode                                                                u:object_r:sysfs_camera_writable:s0
+
 # Module
 genfscon sysfs /module/scsc_bt/parameters/bluetooth_address                                                    u:object_r:sysfs_bt_writable:s0
diff --git a/sepolicy/vendor/hal_camera_default.te b/sepolicy/vendor/hal_camera_default.te
index cf3d50d..026dfea 100644
--- a/sepolicy/vendor/hal_camera_default.te
+++ b/sepolicy/vendor/hal_camera_default.te
@@ -19,3 +19,7 @@ get_prop(hal_camera_default, exported_camera_prop);
 set_prop(hal_camera_default, vendor_camera_prop);
 
 dontaudit hal_camera_default default_prop:file read;
+
+# The first buffer allocation looks up the AIDL allocator; this device only
+# has gralloc 2.0 HIDL, which the HAL then uses, so the lookup can only fail.
+dontaudit hal_camera_default hal_graphics_allocator_service:service_manager find;
